<title>FRANCE: French new housing sales down 4.1 percent in Q3.</title>
<headline>French new housing sales down 4.1 percent in Q3.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of new houses in France fell 4.1 percent in the third quarter from the second, while sales of flats remained stable, provisional figures released by the housing ministry show.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following breakdown:</p>
<p>					    Q3 1996     Q2 1996    Q3 1995</p>
<p>HOUSING</p>
<p>  Put up for sale			 2,481	2,485	2,496</p>
<p>  Sales				     2,321	2,420	2,595</p>
<p>  Stocks				    8,065	8,033	9,580</p>
<p>  Avg Sale price per unit (Ffr)   815,000    778,000    750,000</p>
<p>  Delay in turnover (months)	  10	   11	   12</p>
<p>APARTMENTS</p>
<p>   Put up for sale		     14,058     13,254     12,857</p>
<p>   Sales				   15,531     15,581     13,358</p>
<p>   Stocks				  59,675     61,874     68,417</p>
<p>   Sale price per unit(Ffr/sq m)   12,491     12,404     12,139</p>
<p>   Delay in turnover (months)	 12	   12	   16</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom 33+1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
